<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian s/adj Jan employment rose 38,400.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian s/adj Jan employment rose 38,400.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally-adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons rose 38,400 in January to 8.44 million, against 8.40 million in December and 8.32 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate was at 8.6 percent, unchanged from December, compared with 8.5 percent in January 1996.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to rise around 10,000 in January, seasonally-adjusted, with the unemployment rate steady at 8.6 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)	 Jan 97	Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.6 pct     8.6 pct	8.5 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.44 million    8.40 million     8.32 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		791,800     794,500	770,000</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.8 pct    63.6 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     9.3 pct     8.7 pct	9.2 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.30 million    8.50 million     8.19 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed		853,800     805,700	831,700</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.2 pct    64.3 pct     63.4 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.6 pct	8.6 pct	8.4 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		8.42 million     8.41 million     8.32 million</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     791,500	793,800	767,700</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.6 pct     63.6 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>The Bureau said that of the 38,400 overall rise in employment, part-time employment rose around 34,900 in January.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
